  "scope": "Only the native verification harness changes: it waits for the actual inspector WebSocket close event before returning from a main-process evaluation, and reports an explicit disconnect failure at a bounded deadline. A real Node inspector probe fails before the fix with CLOSING and passes afterward with CLOSED for success/error and normal process exit. The same failed large-workspace fixture passes all six actual model-comparison checks and normal close. Application/renderer bytes and the original desktop close deadline are unchanged. This does not establish the exact cause of the earlier process-exit delay or complete new-harness source/distribution acceptance."
